{*
	The two head-only ways of saying what a template is given: {parameters}, which
	names them one by one, and {varType}, which types a variable declared
	elsewhere. Nothing in this file may be underlined - in particular a variable
	that {parameters} declares is defined, not undefined.

	{templateType}, the third way, needs a class to point at and is in
	template-type.latte next to it.
*}
{parameters int $limit = 10, string $heading = 'Articles', App\Model\Article[] $articles = []}
{varType App\Model\ArticleFacade $facade}

<h1>{$heading}</h1>
<p>{$limit}</p>

<ul>
	<li n:foreach="$articles as $article">{$article->getTitle()}</li>
</ul>

<p>{$facade->getById(1)?->getTitle()}</p>
